{"title":"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent\" title=\"Tangent\">tangent</a> to a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> are tangent to the circles as shown, and the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />  and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> are congruent. What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/a/f4a115a9c8dc91a741d0149edb037b3cb07f6b01.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); pathpen = linewidth(0.7); pointpen = black; real t=2^0.5; D((0,0)--(4*t,0)--(2*t,8)--cycle); D(CR((2*t,2),2)); D(CR((2*t,5),1)); D(&#39;B&#39;, (0,0),SW); D(&#39;C&#39;,(4*t,0), SE); D(&#39;A&#39;, (2*t, 8), N); D((2*t,2)--(2*t,4)); D((2*t,5)--(2*t,6)); MP(&#39;2&#39;, (2*t,3), W); MP(&#39;1&#39;,(2*t, 5.5), W);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4ef2b62896d8fc15e2d6333dc07f44443676fbd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{35}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 15\\sqrt{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{64}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 16\\sqrt{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 24\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"490\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the centers of the smaller and larger circles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> , respectively.\nLet their tangent points to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively.\nWe can then draw the following diagram:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/d/e7dd38d7d5efd1fe119ba93263f1f91a5d1d40fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); pathpen = linewidth(0.7); pointpen = black; pointfontpen = fontsize(10); real t=2^0.5; D((0,0)--(4*t,0)--(2*t,8)--cycle);  D(CR(D((2*t,2)),2)); D(CR(D((2*t,5)),1)); D(&#39;B&#39;, (0,0),SW); D(&#39;C&#39;,(4*t,0), SE); D(&#39;A&#39;, (2*t, 8), N); pair A = foot((2*t,2),(2*t,8),(4*t,0)), B = foot((2*t,5),(2*t,8),(4*t,0)); D((2*t,0)--(2*t,8)); D((2*t,2)--D(A)); D((2*t,5)--D(B)); D(rightanglemark((2*t,2),A,(4*t,0))); D(rightanglemark((2*t,5),B,(4*t,0))); MP(&#39;2&#39;, (2*t,3), W); MP(&#39;1&#39;,(2*t, 5.5), W); MP(&quot;F&quot;,(2*t,0)); MP(&quot;O_1&quot;,(2*t,5),W); MP(&quot;O_2&quot;,(2*t,2),W); MP(&quot;D&quot;,B,NE); MP(&quot;E&quot;,A,NE); [/asy]\" width=\"248\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32fc6f779b0e8adb2293eb9a7d45b88e899c53dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADO_1 \\sim \\triangle AEO_2 \\sim \\triangle AFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"239\" height=\"16\" />. Using the first pair of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Similar_triangles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Similar triangles\">similar triangles</a>, we write the proportion:\n</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10ada06cd47acf9909068e7654b0ddc0944a8f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AO_1}{AO_2} = \\frac{DO_1}{EO_2} \\Longrightarrow \\frac{AO_1}{AO_1 + 3} = \\frac{1}{2} \\Longrightarrow AO_1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"361\" height=\"42\" /></div>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a6f8df26d8788dc53740f3194e3dddd68447c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = \\sqrt{3^2-1^2} = \\sqrt{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Now using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/80526aa7b1b45ef92b994846479159f4bb9ee065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADO_1 \\sim \\triangle AFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091c4ac75473dc96bea1372a641fa96643f04862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AD}{AF} = \\frac{DO_1}{FC} \\Longrightarrow \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{8} = \\frac{1}{FC} \\Longrightarrow FC = 2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"357\" height=\"41\" /></div>\n<p>Hence, the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/d/dcd6a252bcb196578125be40211d95e06cb54e54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AF \\cdot BC = \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AF \\cdot (2\\cdot CF) = AF \\cdot CF = 8\\left(2\\sqrt{2}\\right) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 16\\sqrt{2}}\\]\" width=\"501\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/d/e7dd38d7d5efd1fe119ba93263f1f91a5d1d40fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); pathpen = linewidth(0.7); pointpen = black; pointfontpen = fontsize(10); real t=2^0.5; D((0,0)--(4*t,0)--(2*t,8)--cycle);  D(CR(D((2*t,2)),2)); D(CR(D((2*t,5)),1)); D(&#39;B&#39;, (0,0),SW); D(&#39;C&#39;,(4*t,0), SE); D(&#39;A&#39;, (2*t, 8), N); pair A = foot((2*t,2),(2*t,8),(4*t,0)), B = foot((2*t,5),(2*t,8),(4*t,0)); D((2*t,0)--(2*t,8)); D((2*t,2)--D(A)); D((2*t,5)--D(B)); D(rightanglemark((2*t,2),A,(4*t,0))); D(rightanglemark((2*t,5),B,(4*t,0))); MP(&#39;2&#39;, (2*t,3), W); MP(&#39;1&#39;,(2*t, 5.5), W); MP(&quot;F&quot;,(2*t,0)); MP(&quot;O_1&quot;,(2*t,5),W); MP(&quot;O_2&quot;,(2*t,2),W); MP(&quot;D&quot;,B,NE); MP(&quot;E&quot;,A,NE); [/asy]\" width=\"248\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac168761e3eddc1b3ae1d5786fd1aecdecb95d24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{A O_1 D} \\sim \\triangle{A O_2 E},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" /> we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffe5f49ff41927f15b960fd201dba764e76cf957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A O_1}{A O_2} = \\frac{O_1 D}{O_2 E} = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"140\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Since we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cccc92e4c6f69f25637e742ed81ab8af7f30bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1 O_2 = 1 + 2 = 3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"144\" height=\"16\" /> the total length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/899e11a9dc4e364083145ad5eb87be8cf6a0f803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A O_2 = 2 \\cdot 3 = 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84a34c023078cc068ba531b409c780e8dba6f33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2 F = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14f0baab5817bb749a1d1cb6e83e73add3f612a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A F = A O_2 + O_2 F = 6 + 2 = 8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"246\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/4310eee9b620e4646cf61e6c7d7516944da2f4c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABF} \\sim \\triangle{A E O_2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" /> we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffefde884d74dc20d1e7f3f2509eb611d6470c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AC}{A O_2} = \\frac{FC}{O_2 E}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"106\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Since we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/7422d34fdaedc435941b019ccf5e2752f229ce11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A O_2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeeabe73062d87290a941ecf5713b472c4525730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2 E = 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/b/81bae3b81ef46413ae9905f8fbfe044984061532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AC}{6} = \\frac{FC}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This equation simplified gets us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f580c5478a47658be329d8fe86a88fbcd1b0d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 3 \\cdot FC.$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e10f4a272e514fcc1fd3a792fee66e3be7ace7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC = a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb5b2cd7a1ddfa3ae1c753633ffa6a077d14f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AFC},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1eac99539a4d1b63bd594eb17b90cd8c912bf3ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF^2 + FC^2 = AC^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"156\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f11fd78e70b9f9143c3d617e4faf959966a46c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = 8$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e10f4a272e514fcc1fd3a792fee66e3be7ace7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC = a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/d/e4d447bf8bb778325fb63c76a9b9fac523174013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 3a$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/3/0c38c9598abe15fff342b72531367a88df40f962.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^2 + a^2 = (3a)^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e8d3dd88b3f5fba4d263c96deeb69832faf45ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 = 8a^2 \\Rightarrow a^2 = 8 \\Rightarrow a = \\sqrt{8} = 2 \\sqrt{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"294\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/515bb0d545fb6989ea589a9002136e7e91a003f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC=a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f7063b6ff14723e04667035cb0db64b697f09ea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 2 \\cdot FC = 2 \\cdot 2 \\sqrt{2} = 4 \\sqrt{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"245\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df4558749dac946baa16514b8f039577ad5d1533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = 8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> we have the area equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42efc04be5a19b21e39187075fa3caa71c2847c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2} \\cdot 8}{2}=16\\sqrt{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"129\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Thus our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/0270cb4e2f7f4b008824f32c7f9639c1c949669f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16 \\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"91\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the diagram from Solutions 1 and 2, and knowing that the height has length eight, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419dea12de38c0f719dc92765204a7ccb24cd27f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. We get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a5020274d7a2b47238051a24db7365f12771e7e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC = \\sqrt{FC^2 + 64}.\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> We can set up the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e980a8278dc26fc1e24a3d9e079cd5eb5ab3011.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2FC + 2 \\sqrt{FC^2 + 64} = 8FC,\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"20\" /> both sides equal the full perimeter of the triangle. Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815d39fd1cfe5643a3e465aeaefb1052281fb8e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2FC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> from both sides gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d84ccc265a074287f9959c99404b2b8ad61a2ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sqrt{FC^2+64}=6FC.\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" /> Squaring and dividing both sides by four gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c580f8f6e2b7a84c011bfb90748384ffc86402f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC^2 + 64 = 9FC^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7e6fa80dd7cee1a9d06475ea3a2f26c8722bb2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 = 8FC^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" /> This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f190a5d7b0ae2a92d0037bf3de5428e044fbed32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC = 2 \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" />. The whole length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3f43ae8f8f1306b3547283e641e1df970167ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d35a5da7d4975e8cd93bc0d46611746e7a09d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16\\sqrt{2}\\Rightarrow\\boxed{D}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" /> ~booking\n~edits by HM2018\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A\">2006 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Proble